{"duration_api_ms":1666066,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b5b42b1e-07e1-41c2-94e8-556b69ff0215","total_cost_usd":52.664962000000024,"usage":{"input_tokens":538,"cache_creation_input_tokens":311036,"cache_read_input_tokens":89400176,"output_tokens":117588,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":37388},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":311036,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4573,"cache_read_input_tokens":495523,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4195,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4195},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":544,"outputTokens":118291,"thinkingTokens":37526,"cacheReadInputTokens":89521834,"cacheCreationInputTokens":494405,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":52.664962000000024,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":269,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"All work is complete. Final report:\n\n## 1. Per-finding summary\n\n| # | What I changed |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | `assets/linux/DEBIAN/postrm`: `purge` no longer `rm -rf`s `/home/*/…` and `/root/…` app data — it leaves per-user data alone and says so. `prerm`: dropped the system-wide `pkill -x librepili`. |\n| 2 | Added `String.isHttpUrl` (`string_ext.dart`); `PiliScheme._toWebview` now refuses any non-http(s) url, `WebviewPage.initState` falls back to `about:blank` for one (the chokepoint every `/webview` push goes through), and `PageUtils.launchURL` blocks `file/content/javascript/data/blob/about/filesystem` while still handing custom app schemes to the OS. |\n| 3 | `_saveSnapshot` now calls `exportAllSettings()` without credentials (undo restores this device's from the live box, which `importAllJsonSettings` already does), and `GStorage.clear()` deletes the whole `snapshots/` dir. |\n| 4 | `showImportExportDialog.beforeExport` is now `Future<bool>` (false cancels); 登录信息 got a confirm dialog naming SESSDATA/bili_jct/access_key and the clipboard risk; the settings entry returns `true`. |\n| 5 | `Accounts.clear()` now sets `MineController.anonymity = true` and runs `LoginUtils.onLogoutMain()`. |\n| 6 | `loginByCookie` now does the same opt-in sequence as `setAccount`: `loginMode=true` → `Accounts.refresh()` → `anonymity=false` → `onLoginMain()` (or the role dialog). |\n| 7 | `Api.liveFeedback` added to `LoginPolicy._recommendApis`. |\n| 8 | `GrpcUrl.audioPlayList` added to `LoginPolicy._grpcAccountApis`. |\n| 9 | `AnonymousAccount.delete()` sets `activated = false`. |\n| 10 | `Accounts.deleteAll` clears `loginMode` + `anonymity` when the box empties; `MineController.onChangeAnonymity`'s `isEmpty` branch now also turns a leftover `loginMode` off before showing the toast. |\n| 11 | Cross-origin redirect branch now removes every `x-bili-*` header plus `buvid` and `referer` (case-insensitive) rather than an allow-list of four. |\n| 12 | `onLogoutMain` chains `setAnonymousWebCookie()` after `deleteAllCookies()`. |\n| 13 | `LocalCacheKey.timeStamp` is written inside `_getWbiKeys` **on success only**; `_future` cleared on success too; the date branch collapsed accordingly. |\n| 14 | 动态/关注/粉丝 row wrapped in `if (controller.isLogin)`. |\n| 15 | `exportAllSettings` excludes `SettingBoxKey.loginMode`. |\n| 16 | Added `LoginPolicy.isAccountPath(path)`; the 账号模式 dialog marks every row `[带账号]` / `[匿名]` and the blurb explains both. |\n| 17 | The 确定 button collects the `Accounts.set` futures, `await Future.wait`s them and toasts on error. |\n| 18 | New `LoginAccount.dropCredentials()` (drops every cookie except `DedeUserID`/`buvid3`, nulls `accessKey`/`refresh`), called from `markExpired`; `accessKey`/`refresh` made mutable and `csrf` made null-safe so the record still loads. |\n| 19 | The ban-word dialog builds the `RegExp` in a try/catch **before** touching any state, rejects patterns that `hasMatch('')` (stray `\\|`), and toasts instead of half-saving. The four `enableFilter` readers (`RecommendFilter`, `ReplyGrpc`, `DynamicsDataModel`, `VideoHttp`) also ignore an empty-matching pattern persisted by an older build. |\n| 20 | Every `int.parse` in `app_scheme.dart` → `int.tryParse` with null handling (+ a `pathSegments.length < 4` guard); new `IdUtils.bv2avOrNull` returns null for out-of-alphabet BV chars and is used on the deep-link path. |\n| 21 | `_connectDm` schedules the backoff on **any** token failure; `lib/tcp/live.dart` requires `totalSize >= 16` before recursing. |\n| 22 | The `mt:*` gate now requires `uri.authority == <this provider's authority>` and that the documentId resolves under this provider's root. |\n| 23 | `HomeController.setTabConfig` treats an empty `tabBarSort` as \"use the defaults\". |\n| 24 | About-page import toasts the snapshot path; a 恢复到导入前 entry added next to it; `restoreLatestSnapshot` now snapshots the state it replaces (undo is repeatable/reversible). |\n| 25 | `patch.ps1` resolves `material_ui`/`cupertino_ui` from the version in `pubspec.lock` instead of a name glob, and only rewrites the global git identity when `$env:GITHUB_ACTIONS -eq \"true\"`. |\n| 26 | `build.yml`: signing guard checks all four secrets, secrets go through `env:` instead of inline interpolation, dead `pull_request`/upstream-repo gates and the dev-apk step removed. `build.gradle.kts`: a `key.properties` with `storeFile` but a missing password/alias now fails the build. `linux_x64.yml`: `permissions: contents: write`, `inputs.tag` instead of `github.event.inputs.tag`, two no-op `sed` calls removed. |\n| 27 | All 27 git `ref:` descriptors in `pubspec.yaml` pinned to the `resolved-ref` SHAs from the lock (branch kept as a trailing comment); re-ran `flutter pub get` — every `resolved-ref` is unchanged. |\n| 28 | `SendMessage` → `SendMessageTimeoutW(..., SMTO_ABORTIFHUNG, 3000, …)`, falling back to starting normally. |\n| 29 | Null-check on the decoded avatar, falling back to `R.mipmap.ic_launcher`. |\n| 30 | Added `Utils.secureRandom = Random.secure()`, used for both `blockUserID` generation sites; `_isBlockServer` now requires host **and** the `blockServer` path prefix. |\n| 31 | **No change** — see uncertainty list; the premise does not hold. |\n| 32 | `reply_menu_helper` builds the rule with `caseSensitive: false`, matching `ReplyGrpc` and the settings dialog. |\n| 33 | Both timecode formatters round to whole milliseconds first, then decompose; `dateFormat` handles `diff.isNegative` explicitly. |\n| 34 | `DateUtils.isSameDay(selectedDate, nowDate)`. |\n| 35 | `MIXED_CONTENT_ALWAYS_ALLOW` → `MIXED_CONTENT_COMPATIBILITY_MODE`. |\n| 36 | Documented the limitation (`desktop_webview_window` has no set-cookie API; only `getAllCookies`/`clearAll`), taking the finding's \"accept and document it\" branch. |\n| 37 | **Reverted** — see uncertainty list. |\n| 38 | Corrected the stale `fixerA-resume.txt:71` claim; it now says the feature is on and names the fingerprint. |\n\n## 2. `git diff`\n\nThe full cumulative diff is in the four chunks printed above (workflows/android/assets/scripts/windows; `lib/utils/accounts*`, `app_scheme`, `string_ext`, `id_utils`; remaining `lib/utils` + `grpc`/`http`/`tcp`/`models`; `lib/pages` + `lib/common`; `pubspec.yaml` + the audit report). Total: **47 files, +562 / −209**, excluding `pubspec.lock` (27 `ref:` descriptor lines regenerated by `flutter pub get`, every `resolved-ref` byte-identical) and `audit-logs/route-pending.md` / `ld.txt`, which were already dirty before this session.\n\n## 3. Uncertainty list\n\n- **Finding 31 — no change made, premise disproved.** I measured it: with `RetryInterceptor(dio, 2, 1)` and an always-failing adapter, an interceptor registered *after* it sees the error **exactly once** (adapter called 3×, `onError seen=1`). The innermost recursion level already calls `handler.next(err)`, which is what reaches `AccountManager.onError` — so `toast(err)` and `_saveCookies` *do* run. Switching the outer `handler.reject` → `handler.next` raised it to **3** (one toast/`_saveCookies` per retry level). dio 5.11.1 confirms it: `errorInterceptorWrapper` `throw`s on `reject` and continues on `next`. Left as-is; the probe test was deleted.\n- **Finding 37 — reverted after implementing it.** I wrote the coalescing, then found `ReplyController.queryBySortType()` and `PageOrderMixin.updatePageOrder()` mutate a parameter and then call `onReload()`. Sharing an in-flight refresh would serve data fetched with the *old* sort/order while the UI already shows the new one. The finding itself calls the current behaviour \"Correct\" and conditions the fix on \"if traffic matters\", so I chose correctness. A safe version would need per-parameter keying, which is beyond \"smallest change\" — flagging for your call.\n- **Finding 35 (geetest) — unverified.** I made the one-line change as asked but **cannot verify the captcha still loads**: that needs a real login attempt on a device. If geetest serves any asset over plain http, this will break login. Easy to revert.\n- **Finding 26 (gradle) — deliberately narrower than the literal ask.** I did *not* make the release variant fail outright when no signing config exists; that would break `flutter build apk --release` for any contributor without `key.properties`. Instead the CI guard now requires all four secrets, and gradle fails when `key.properties` is half-configured. If you want the hard CI-only failure too, say so.\n- **Finding 3** — excluding credentials from the snapshot means an undo of an import that *replaced* the WebDAV password restores the pre-import settings but keeps the **imported** password. That is exactly the \"restoring them from the live box\" semantics the auditor proposed, but it is a small fidelity loss in that one case.\n- **Finding 18** — `csrf` now returns `''` instead of throwing when `bili_jct` is gone. Logging out an already-expired account server-side (`LoginHttp.logout`) will now send an empty csrf and fail cleanly rather than throwing; the account is still removed locally.\n- **Finding 2** — `launchURL` uses a denylist, not the literal http/https allowlist, because `webview/view.dart:146,160` deliberately hands custom app schemes (`weixin://`, `bilibili://`…) to the OS; an allowlist would break that. `_toWebview` and the WebView itself *do* use a strict http(s) allowlist.\n- **Finding 22** — the authority check is provably correct; I did not try to verify the auditor's own hypothesis about AOSP's same-uid grant fast path (they noted the hole doesn't depend on it).\n- **Finding 27** — `pubspec.lock` is now regenerated; CI's `flutter pub get` will produce the same file.\n- **Finding 20** — one behaviour change beyond pure guarding: `bilibili://video/123?cid=abc` used to throw, now falls through to the `videoPush` (no-cid) branch instead of doing nothing.\n\n## 4. TEST RESULTS\n\n```\nTEST RESULTS:\n  runner: flutter test (+ dart analyze)\n  command: dart analyze lib test && flutter test\n  exit_code: 0\n  total: 102\n  passed: 102\n  failed: 0\n  skipped: 0\n  duration_ms: ~2500 (flutter test); analyze ~40000\n\nINFRA REPAIRS (during auto-repair, empty if none):\n  (none)\n\nREAL FAILURES (audit-fix-caused regressions, empty if none):\n  (none)\n\nINFRA-PERSISTENT (failures that hit the 3-cycle repair cap, empty if none):\n  (none)\n\nOVERALL: PASS\n```\n\n`dart analyze lib test` reports 36 issues, all `info`-level and all pre-existing, in vendored widget copies (`lib/common/widgets/flutter/**`, `lib/pages/dynamics/widgets/vote_decoration.dart`) — none in any file this pass touched, and no errors or warnings. `dart format` was run on all 37 touched Dart files.","ttft_ms":4802,"type":"result","duration_ms":2841834,"uuid":"e83d777c-dbbc-44af-b1ee-86981b28b4e8","ttft_stream_ms":4467,"time_to_request_ms":471,"first_content_frame_ms":4468,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
